    "field": "Cryospheric hydrology",
    "problem": "Accurately modeling the hydrological impact of climate change in Himalayan catchments is complex due to data scarcity, large uncertainties in climate projections, and existing models that fail to explicitly simulate the coupled evolution of glaciers and other major hydrological processes.",
    "method": "A high-resolution, combined cryospheric-hydrological model is proposed to assess climate change impacts by explicitly simulating glacier evolution and major hydrological processes, forced by an ensemble of downscaled climate model data in a Himalayan catchment.",
    "task": "The task is to assess the future evolution of glaciers and runoff in a glacierized Himalayan catchment using a combined cryospheric hydrological model forced with an ensemble of downscaled climate model data.",
